      "text": "Methadone for opioid addiction:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " give the first dose under supervision when there are no signs of sedation or intoxication and withdrawal symptoms are present; an initial 20 to 30 mg will often suppress withdrawal, and the initial dose should not exceed 30 mg; the first day's total should not ordinarily exceed 40 mg."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
